<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chauhan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chahamanas, Chauhan Rajputs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chauhans are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clan of northern and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, descended in tradition from the Chahamana dynasties that ruled Shakambhari and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a>, whose best-known king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraj Chauhan</a>, fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> in 1192. Branches of the clan later ruled many smaller states in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, several of which survived as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> until 1948.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Beyond this core the emperors ruled through feudatory dynasties, the samantas, who governed their own lands, paid tribute and sent troops; among them were the <b>Chahamanas</b> of Shakambhari, the Guhilas, the Chandela dynasty, the Kalachuris and the Chalukyas of Saurashtra.</blockquote><a href="/empire/gurjara-pratihara">Gurjara-Pratihara · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>When Mahmud Begada of the Gujarat Sultanate took Champaner and Pavagadh in 1484, the defeated <b>Chauhan Rajput</b> rulers' descendants withdrew into the hills to the east.</blockquote><a href="/state/baria-state">Baria State</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1342 Rao Deva, of the Hada branch of the <b>Chauhans</b>, took the Bundi area from local Meena chiefs and made it his capital.</blockquote><a href="/state/bundi-state">Bundi State</a></li><li><blockquote>The Jalor branch of the <b>Chahamanas</b> (Chauhans) descended from the Chahamanas of Naddula.</blockquote><a href="/state/chahamanas-of-jalor">Chahamanas of Jalor</a></li><li><blockquote>The Naddula <b>Chahamanas</b> held the southern Marwar plains and the routes between Gujarat and the north.</blockquote><a href="/state/chahamanas-of-naddula">Chahamanas of Naddula</a></li><li><blockquote>His descendants ruled there as a separate <b>Chauhan</b> line.</blockquote><a href="/state/chahamanas-of-ranastambhapura">Chahamanas of Ranastambhapura</a></li></ul></section>
